# KIRA — Long-Endurance ISR / Counter-UAS Aircraft

KIRA was a one-year **conceptual and preliminary aircraft-design project** at Politecnico di Milano for a long-endurance fixed-wing ISR platform with integrated Counter-UAS capability.

The baseline concept targeted approximately **25 hours of endurance with a 125 kg mission payload**, integrating radar, EO/IR, EW, communications and a deployable ground-control architecture.

## My Role

**Team Leader — 5-member engineering team**

I was responsible for project and technical coordination and contributed directly to:

- mission requirements, CONOPS and system architecture;
- aircraft configuration trade-offs and preliminary sizing;
- propulsion, performance, mass, power and CG integration;
- radar, EO/IR and EW payload integration;
- preliminary structural sizing and load assessment;
- mobile GCS concept and aircraft-level multidisciplinary integration.

KIRA remained at preliminary-design maturity; no full-scale prototype was built.

> **Public-material note:** only selected material suitable for public distribution is included here. Detailed calculations, design data and internal project files are not public and cannot be shared in this repository.
